# Nibras process security (ADR-0045 / NPS-1 / NPS-2 / NPS-3)

- Process YAML `human_only` / `separation_of_duties` / `refuse_if` = **Pulse dials**, not host ACL alone.
- Host SoD: leave/loan/**attendance ESS** via Correspondence; payroll commit / GOSI submit / onboarding activate via **`people.governance.sod`**. Attendance admin PATCH remains SoD-gated ops fallback.
- Stamp preparer on staging (compute/generate/create); refuse on irreversible (commit/submit/activate/approve). Wire **DRF + host_executor** — never Agent-only.
- **NPS-2:** Pulse inbox `required_authority` for Nibras `*.review` via **`ai.governance.review_authority`** → `correspondence:act` / `correspondence:finance` / `people:manage`.
- **NPS-3:** Attendance happy path = `POST /me/attendance-permissions/` + manager corr (`people.attendance_ess`); Agent tools `submit_my_attendance_permission`.
- **Forbidden:** scattered per-view SoD one-offs; ORM bypass of SoD; inventing Django perms from capability `permissions:` lists.
- Honesty matrix CI: `ai/tests/test_nibras_process_security_planes.py` · host tests: `people/tests/test_host_sod.py` · review authority: `ai/tests/test_review_authority.py` · ESS: `people/tests/test_attendance_ess.py`.
- Read: `.ai-toolkit/decisions/0045-nibras-process-security-planes.md` · `shared/security.md` RULE 11 · PB-61 · RULE_34.
